{contentTitle}\". Clear examples, important terms and statements, interesting facts, life applications.`",{"type":16,"value":118},"Connections",{"type":21,"value":120},"(contentTitle) => `Summary of the topic \"${contentTitle}\": key definitions, theorems, properties and examples of their use. All the most important things in a concise form!`",{"type":16,"value":122},"Key elements",{"type":16,"value":124},"Need to know",{"type":21,"value":126},"(contentTitle) => `Various problems with hints and answers on the topic \"${contentTitle}\". Interesting conditions, hints and detailed solutions. Turn knowledge into a skill!`",{"type":16,"value":128},"Depends on",{"type":16,"value":130},"Used by",{"type":16,"value":132},"Externals",{"m":134},"function m(number, one, few, includeNumber = true) {\n  const text = number === 1 ? one : few;\n  return includeNumber ? `${number} ${text}` : text;\n}",{"contentPath":136,"mainContent":137},"group/foundations/equations/",{"fullId":138,"shortId":138,"contentRelativePath":139,"title":140,"bookTitle":9,"breadcrumbs":141,"description":144,"stats":145,"connections":152,"contributions":163,"type":168,"children":169},"foundations/equations","01-foundations/02-equations","Equations",[142],{"icon":143,"title":9,"link":11},"book-outline","\n        Analysis of the most popular equations: elementary, quadratic, systems, etc.\n        You will understand why they need to be solved at all and how they can be used to describe processes in real life.\n        We will also consider nuances: transformations, domain restrictions, \"loss\" and appearance of \"extraneous\" roots, and many others.\n    ",{"materials":146,"elements":147},2,{"accent_term":148,"accent_statement":149,"accent_important":150,"problem":151},3,1,4,35,{"externals":153},[154],{"type":155,"title":9,"items":156},"parent",[157],{"type":158,"title":159,"info":160,"link":161,"reason":162},"web","LibreTexts Mathematics","An open and free online collection of mathematics educational materials.","https://math.libretexts.org/","A large amount of materials and many typical practice problems.",[164],{"contributorId":165,"name":166,"avatarUrl":167},"gwynerva","Peter Radko","/file/contributors/gwynerva/avatar.png","group",[170,250],{"type":171,"link":172,"title":173,"description":174,"quickLinks":175,"stats":248},"topic","/article/foundations/equations/elementary/","Elementary Equations","\n        We will learn how to solve elementary equations and transform equalities.\n        Simple, visual, with examples and without memorizing a bunch of strange rules.\n        This is a key and necessary skill in mathematics and all other exact sciences.\n    ",[176,184,191,198,205,212,220,227,234,241],{"link":177,"schemaName":178,"title":179,"quick":180,"seo":181,"description":183},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equality","accent_term","Equality",{},{"title":182},"What is equality?","Two expressions with an equals sign \"=\" between them. Equality can be true (2 = 2) or false (2 = 0).",{"link":185,"schemaName":186,"title":187,"quick":188,"seo":189,"description":190},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equality-false-true","diagram","True and false equality",{},{},"If identical objects stand on the sides of the = sign, then the equality is true. If different — false.",{"link":192,"schemaName":178,"title":193,"quick":194,"seo":195,"description":197},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equation","Equation",{},{"title":196},"What is an equation?","An equality in which there is one or more unknowns or variables.",{"link":199,"schemaName":178,"title":200,"quick":201,"seo":202,"description":204},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equation-solution","Solving an Equation",{},{"title":203},"What does it mean to solve an equation?","\"Solutions\" or \"roots\" of an equation are numbers that, when substituted for unknowns, turn it into a true equality.\n                    \"To solve an equation\" means to find all its roots and prove that there are no other roots.",{"link":206,"schemaName":207,"title":208,"quick":209,"seo":210,"description":211},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#same-action-rule","accent_statement","Same Action Rule",{},{},"If the same action is performed on both sides of a true equality, the resulting equality will also be true.",{"link":213,"schemaName":214,"title":215,"quick":216,"seo":217,"description":219},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#common-mistakes","list","Mistakes when solving equations",{},{"title":218},"Common mistakes when solving equations","A list of common mistakes that beginners make when solving equations.",{"link":221,"schemaName":222,"title":223,"quick":224,"seo":225,"description":226},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#why-solve-equations-1","heading","Why Solve Equations?",{},{},"A set of examples requiring the ability to solve equations to work with.",{"link":228,"schemaName":222,"title":229,"quick":230,"seo":231,"description":233},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#triangle-of-formulas","Triangle of Formulas",{},{"title":232},"Magic triangle of formulas","A mnemonic technique for memorizing simple formulas.",{"link":235,"schemaName":222,"title":236,"quick":237,"seo":238,"description":240},"/article/foundations/equations/elementary/#equations-in-life","Equations in Life",{},{"title":239},"Where are equations used in life?","A selection of problems and situations from real life that can be solved if translated into equations.",{"link":242,"schemaName":243,"title":244,"quick":245,"seo":246,"description":247},"/practice/foundations/equations/elementary/#linear-root","problems","Linear equations formula",{},{},"Formula by which you can very quickly find the root of any equation of the form Ax + B = 0.",{"elements":249},{"accent_term":148,"accent_statement":149,"accent_important":150,"problem":151},{"type":168,"link":251,"title":252,"stats":253},"/group/foundations/equations/quadratic/","Quadratic Equations",{"materials":149},{"contributorsCount":149,"sponsorsCount":255},0,{"shortBookId":5,"frontNav":257},{"type":8,"shortId":5,"title":9,"flags":258,"link":11,"children":259},{},[260],{"type":168,"separator":261,"shortId":138,"title":140,"flags":262,"link":263,"children":264},true,{},"/group/foundations/equations/",[265,268],{"type":171,"shortId":266,"title":173,"flags":267,"link":172},"foundations/equations/elementary",{},{"type":168,"separator":269,"shortId":270,"title":252,"flags":271,"link":251,"children":272},false,"foundations/equations/quadratic",{},[273],{"type":171,"shortId":274,"title":275,"flags":276,"link":277},"foundations/equations/quadratic/basics","Quadratic Equations Basics",{},"/article/foundations/equations/quadratic/basics/",1769364889887]